      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A \"stone in the pond\" strategy is a practical approach to investigating large-scale nosocomial tuberculosis (TB) exposures. Here, we describe such a risk-stratified approach to contact tracing after a TB exposure that occurred over 5 months in a pediatric inpatient ward in a country with a moderate TB burden. Infect Control Hosp Epidemiol 2017;38:1509-1511."},
